"""Default terrain smoke: a survival world on the default terrain (run it with --gamemode survival --difficulty normal
--preset normal; the seed is the run's, 31 by default), its chunks generated by walking a spectator step by step
(teleports, never one large forceload), the region files of the overworld and the nether counted after the world was
left (scan_region.py), and a short survival opening in the same world with real actions: logs by hand, planks, crafting
tables, sticks and a wooden pickaxe crafted with real slot clicks, one HBM ore and eight stone mined, a furnace crafted
and placed, the ore smelted into an ingot. Then the world is left and opened again and the same server readings
compared.

The block list is the world-generation handover of the main-line closure report (WORLDGEN below, its rows copied: block,
biome tag, placed feature, placing code, config gates with their defaults, on by default). Lower-bound rule, one for the
whole list: AT LEAST ONE block of each listed block in the scanned chunks of its dimension, with these exceptions:
- off by default (the nether plutonium ore, CommonConfig.java:693-696, original GeneralConfig.java:99): asserted ABSENT;
- End-only (tikite, ore_tikite_placed in add_end_ores): outside this smoke, not run;
- rare per-chunk events (oil bubble 1/100, bedrock oil, landmine, crashed bomb 1/500, alexandrite 1/100, blueprint
  chest): the scan size N is chosen so that finding none is unlikely; a block found passes, a block not found is left
  for a person with the probability of finding none in N chunks, not recorded as a world-generation fault;
- noise-placed regions (schist stratum and the schist ores in it, the hematite, bauxite and malachite layers): a block
  not found is left for a person as a scan-range question.
N: the crashed bomb is the rarest per-chunk event of the list (RarityFilter 500, NtmPlacedFeatures.java:112; original
WorldConfig.java:87 dudSpawn 500, HbmWorldGen.java:241); (499/500)^N <= 1 % needs N >= 2,300 chunks in which a bomb could
stand, so the walk generates a 4 x 4 grid of view areas (about 3,200 chunks) around the spawn. The blueprint chest can only
generate in chunks whose corner lies within the first 16 blocks of a 5,000-block grid cell outside the spawn square
(BlueprintChestFeature.java:36-44,55-57; original HbmWorldGen.java:483-490), half of them: eight such chunks are visited,
P(none) = 0.5^8 = 0.4 %. The coltan deposit is one square per world around a centre computed from the seed
(ColtanDepositFeature.java:47-52; original HbmWorldGen.java:159-162): the walk visits the centre.
A sand oil bubble among the scan's oil spills (oily sand around the spill, tar sand just below it) is looked at from above and over its shaft after
the reopen: two pictures for a person (original MapGenBubble.java:93-134,148-174).
"""
